## 📋 Configuration Summary

### PostgreSQL Service
- **Status**: Automatic startup enabled
- **Port**: 5432
- **User**: postgres (no password on localhost)
- **Location**: C:\Program Files\PostgreSQL\18\

### Database
- **Name**: auth_api
- **Authentication**: Trust (no password localhost)
- **Persistence**: Permanent in C:\Program Files\PostgreSQL\18\data\

### Performance
- **Max Connections**: 200
- **Shared Buffers**: 256MB
- **Cache Size**: 1GB
- **Optimized for**: Development workloads

### Backups
- **Location**: D:\Odoo Hackathon\backend\db_backups\
- **Manual**: Run `backup-database.ps1` anytime
- **Automatic**: Optional (use `setup-backup-scheduler.ps1`)
- **Retention**: 30 days

---

## 🎯 Implementation Checklist

### Initial Setup
- [ ] Read [QUICK_START.md](QUICK_START.md)
- [ ] Run `setup-postgresql-complete.ps1` as Admin
- [ ] Run `verify-postgresql-setup.ps1` to confirm

### Backend Development
- [ ] Start backend with `npm run dev`
- [ ] Create some test data
- [ ] Verify data persists after backend restart

### (Optional) Automated Backups
- [ ] Run `setup-backup-scheduler.ps1` as Admin
- [ ] Verify task runs with `Get-ScheduledTask -TaskName "PostgreSQL-Database-Backup-auth_api"`

### Data Protection
- [ ] Manually test backup: `& "backup-database.ps1"`
- [ ] Manually test restore: `& "restore-database.ps1"` with test backup
- [ ] Document backup location for team

